      "id": "KA-C60-cow",
      "sequence": 1840,
      "title": "ಹಸು (hasu) — a cow",
      "headword": "ಹಸು",
      "romanization": "hasu",
      "gloss": "a cow",
      "script": "kannada",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:29d490b4ed47dc5d",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did kesaru mean, and what did beṅki mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಸು (hasu) — \"a cow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಸು (hasu) is inherited, and it is the animal a Karnataka household is built around. The ಹಾಲು you met in the drinks chapter comes out of it, and most of what a Kannada kitchen makes begins with what comes out of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It belongs to the ರೈತ before it belongs to anybody, and in a ಹಳ್ಳಿ it is tied in the yard rather than kept in a shed, close enough to the ಬಾಗಿಲು that you step around it going in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಸು (hasu) comes from Sanskrit paśu, \"domestic animal\" (CDIAL 7984), through a Prakrit form pasu. It came in early enough to go through the same change as native words: the p- became h-. This is a tadbhava, a loan reshaped by Kannada sounds."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five animals."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "hasu",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *hasu*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "hasu, then hālu, and say which one comes out of the other",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *hasu*, then *hālu*, and say which one comes out of the other]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say svalpa",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *svalpa*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does ಹಸು (hasu) mean? (\"a cow\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
