        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕೋಳಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) — \"a hen\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) is the domestic fowl, hen or cock alike; the word does not divide them, and where the difference matters a second word goes in front of it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the clock of the ಹಳ್ಳಿ. A ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) wakes a house before ಬೆಳಗ್ಗೆ is properly under way, which is a large part of why nobody there needed a ಗಂಟೆ to do the same job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) is native Dravidian, one word with Tamil kōḻi and Telugu kōḍi (DEDR 2248). DEDR gives the older Kannada kōḻi."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three."
            }
          ]
        },
