      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f7d64ccd45ea377c",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did kāge mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಹಕ್ಕಿ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki) — \"a bird\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki) is the general one: any bird at all, the ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi) and the ಕಾಗೆ (kāge) both inside it. It is Kannada's own, and it sits beside a borrowed word that covers the same ground more formally — the arrangement you already saw when ಸ್ನೇಹಿತ turned out to have ಗೆಳೆಯ living quietly beside it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One warning before you say it out loud. Written in our letters, hakki is akki with an h on the front, and ಅಕ್ಕಿ is the raw rice from the water-and-rice chapter. In Kannada letters they start differently and there is no danger; in a romanization there is. Say the h."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki) comes from Sanskrit pakṣin, \"winged; bird\", through Prakrit pakkhi (CDIAL 7636). It is a tadbhava, old enough that its p- went the way of native p-, to h-."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: ಹಸು (hasu), ಮೇಕೆ (mēke), ಕೋಳಿ (kōḷi), ಕಾಗೆ (kāge), ಹಕ್ಕಿ (hakki). Enough to greet a house and name what lives in it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
